SUMMARY:Learn: Matrix Algebra
LOCATION:
DESCRIPTION:Proof rules\, subspaces\, sums\, unions\, counterexamples\n09:0
 0 Map the course (15 min): Skim the topic list and every overview\, glance
  at one past exam to see the question types (do not solve it)\, and rate e
 ach topic 1-3. Your ratings steer the extra time.\n09:15 Pre-test (10 min)
 : Attempt one problem on this topic cold\, before reading anything. Gettin
 g it wrong is fine: trying first makes the explanation stick.\n09:25 Conce
 pt overview (15 min): Read the overview\, then write the key definitions w
 ord for word from memory. Proofs fail on fuzzy definitions.\n09:40 Worked 
 examples (25 min): For each proof write its skeleton (assumption\, goal\, 
 key step) and why the key step works. Then close it and rebuild the proof 
 from the skeleton.\n10:05 Practice (45 min): Prove the statements yourself
  in full sentences. Stuck: unfold the definitions\, try a small case\, or 
 look for a counterexample.\n10:50 Blank-page recall (10 min): From memory:
  definitions\, theorem statements with all their conditions\, and one coun
 terexample for each condition.
END:VEVENT
