DESCRIPTION:Techniques refresher: parts\, substitution\, trig identities + 
 Definite integrals: absolute value\, piecewise\, substitution limits\n11:3
 0 Map the course (15 min): Skim the topic list and every overview\, glance
  at one past exam to see the question types (do not solve it)\, and rate e
 ach topic 1-3. Your ratings steer the extra time.\n11:45 Pre-test (10 min)
 : Attempt one problem on this topic cold\, before reading anything. Gettin
 g it wrong is fine: trying first makes the explanation stick.\n11:55 Conce
 pt overview (15 min): Read the beginner overview once\, then close it and 
 write from memory: what problem this topic solves\, the key formula or ide
 a\, and when to use it.\n12:10 Worked examples (25 min): Study the worked 
 examples line by line and say why each step is allowed. Then cover the sol
 ution and redo the example yourself.\n12:35 Practice (45 min): Solve from 
 easy to exam level\, writing every step. Check each answer: differentiate 
 the antiderivative\, sanity-check sign and size. After 10 minutes stuck\, 
 uncover only the next line.\n13:20 Blank-page recall (10 min): Blank page:
  write today's formulas and traps from memory\, check\, and copy what you 
 missed to the formula sheet draft and the mistakes log.
END:VEVENT
